e old gate's ids from `c3_tables_round1_audit_legit_leak.md` and `check4a_legit_table.tsv` by shape and say which rows you did not run. The builder claims a reconstruction of the 56 reproduces the gate's head outcome on all 122 trailing cells (50 red, 72 accepted): re-derive, do not trust. (c) **Red by design, reported with the red message (never a defect by themselves):** a step added, removed, renamed, reordered or repeated; a `name:` added to a previously nameless pinned step (the triple changes: red by design, B716-7); a quote added around a step name; a new env key (job or step); a new job-level key. For each: the red test, the message, whether the message tells the editor the exact change (the pinned list line to edit). (d) **The trailing-comment table, rebuilt:** the 61 line kinds x (1 space, 2 spaces) = 122 plants of the round-1 gate, each on the base, round-1 head and head reader (and both interpreters): **predicted: the head red set equals the round-1 head red set on all 122, and every paragraph of the docstring ("accepted at both", "accepted at one space only: timeout-minutes, fail-fast, part: [...], PART:", "a failure at either: ...") true against it**; a contradicted row is an M4. Add the plants the new identity makes new: a ` # note` after a `uses:` value and after a one-line `run:` value (accepted), `#` WITHOUT a space before it inside a one-line `run:` (a value character: red), ` #` inside a `name:`. (e) **Python:** the whole battery of (a) to (c) once under `/usr/bin/python3` 3.9.6 as well as 3.14.7: the red sets are equal (control: a difference is printed if one is planted).

