## SEVERITY / VERDICT (the grading rule is decided HERE; apply it, do not re-argue it)
*Blocker:* a path beyond the one; a commit count other than 2 or a second commit that is not the builder's one path; a workflow, product, web, Api or other-infra byte; a head blob other than `a183d2ac`; an existing statement of main's reader changed, removed or made conditional (Check 1 AST comparison; the two named added assertion lines excepted); **a loosening: a plant that was red at the base or round-1 reader and is green at the head reader**; a non-ASCII byte, a person's name, a decision-card id, a `B###` token or a ticket key written whole in an added line or a commit message; a skip, sleep, retry, environment or provider gate; an import, file access, subprocess or network call added; the head reader not 34 ran or red on the unmutated `ci.yml` (blob `0176b491`) or on main's; **the suite red through `test_security_baseline.py`, `ResourceWarnings` above 0 or files still open above 0 in either interpreter or either tree (CI's predicate)**; names lost above 0 or added other than the three; a `__pycache__` left in a tree by the reader; the head moved; **a red or cancelled check-run that is NOT the environmental Pkcs pair as decided in Check 7 (D3)**; a CodeQL alert open on the head (either threshold), a missing analysis at the verdict, or an alert dismissed other than by the org; a textual conflict in Check 8; a secret.
*Major, class SAME (the class is "closing the open lists of the shard-job reader"):* **(M1) a LEAK of a route the lane names, MEASURED on this head:** an edit meeting the PROPERTY's first half (adds, removes, renames, reorders or repeats a step; changes WHICH ACTION a pinned `uses:` step runs or WHICH COMMAND a pinned one-line `run:` step runs; gives a step a `name:` equal to a pinned identity while it runs something else; adds an environment name through the file's structure; repeats a job-level key or writes a block key in the flow style; repeats a proof name) that leaves all 34 tests green and is not shown equivalent by a run or by the workflow's semantics. **Decided here (D4):** the bodies of the unread steps, the ref after the `@`, `with:` inputs (including `repository:` and `source-url:`), `if:`, `id`, `timeout-minutes`, `working-directory`, `shell: sh`, env VALUES, `runs-on` and the job's `defaults.run.working-directory` are the NAMED RESIDUE: the commission pins none of them and the docstring says so; a GREEN on them is NOT an M1, whatever the effect, as long as the docstring sentence naming it is true (the effect of a hostile `with:` input or body is the candidate "closed-shape lane for unread bodies and inputs", ticketed, not this PR's). **(M2) a pin that turns a legitimate or routine edit red** (the "must stay green" classes of Check 4(b)) when the red message does not name the exact change, or any such edit an automatic updater makes without a human reading the test; **(M3) a loosening in substance:** an existing assertion made weaker in meaning without a changed line (a helper that now returns less), or a round-1 pin the round-2 commit dropped; **(M4) a docstring sentence that states a measured fact the repository contradicts** (a trailing-comment row, a "free" or "accepted" claim, a soft-pin list entry that is not pinned, a pin that is claimed and absent, a "not read" item that a plant shows IS read, a "caught" claim that a plant shows is not); **(M5) an assertion of the sweep whose removal leaves every plant green, that guards a property of the PROPERTY, and for which YOU build a plant that leaks past it.** A Major SAME here means NO GO and the CAP: before you write it, re-run the plant from a clean layout, print its diff against `ci.yml` and the run's output, and prove the anchor count and the restore.
*Major, class DIFFERENT:* a builder claim contradicted by measurement with a verdict consequence (24 of 24 forgery plants, 178 of 178 legitimate rows, 34 ran, names lost 0 added 0, whole-infra 262, the 3.9 result, the AST figures): if your figures contradict the builder's the verdict carries the contradiction.
*Minor / Note (never a Major, never a NO GO):* the NAMED residue (above) while the sentence naming it is TRUE; an understated or imprecise docstring sentence that characterises the unread remainder (Minor, with the exact rewording); the by-design reds when the red message names the first difference (listed once with the fix: an edit of `PINNED_STEPS` or a key tuple beside the workflow edit); the split ticket-key stem at line 461; the four Bicep `setUpClass` errors without the binary (a base fact when your base run shows the same four); the 3.9.6 whole-infra failure when it is the same at base; GitHub's handling of a duplicate mapping key, of the env name `BASH_FUNC_exit%%`, of a skipped step or of a forged `uses:` UNMEASURED; the runner's Python UNMEASURED; 10 repeats instead of 20; the PR title's ticket key and the STALE PR body (the squash message and body are Tuesday's); the unsigned commits; the `Opus` versus `Sonnet` wording of the attribution line in the PR body versus the commit; the CRLF behaviour (information); the environmental `api` red as decided in Check 7.
*Where the line between Note and Major is unclear:* a thing that makes a PINNED step able to change which action or command it runs while the tests stay green, or turns a routine edit red without telling the editor what to change, is at least Major SAME; a thing that changes only what a message or a comment says and stays true is a Note; a thing in the NAMED residue is a Note. Say which rule you applied for every finding.
**VERDICT RULES.** GO needs Checks 1 to 9 clean and measured, both CodeQL thresholds met on a COMPLETE scan (4 of 4 analyses at `22d5c13`, 0 open alerts), every check-run `completed` `success` (the CodeQL umbrella included), the whole-infra run CI's way green in both trees, 0 findings above Note. **While any check-run of the head is pending the verdict is at most GO WITH FINDINGS and carries `(conditional: CI pending: <names>)`, never a bare GO; while the three `api` checks are red for the environmental Pkcs pair it is at most GO WITH FINDINGS carrying `(conditional: CI red, environmental: <names>)`.** GO WITH FINDINGS = Minor/Note only (plus the environmental red). NO GO on any Blocker or Major SAME and it is the CAP: STATUS gives each Major's plant (diff against `ci.yml`), the red set by name (or "none: green"), your run's output and a fix-shape in prose, and FOR TUESDAY says what ships (the closed instances: the routes of the old gate, the key sets, the duplicate-key refusal, the distinct names, the triple identity wherever it holds) and what is ticketed with your cells attached. NOT GATED = the head moved, the PR is not open, or a moved guarded region. A security-shaped finding is a STOP for tier 1.
