d to <sha7>> - Jira <HPSMPOC-353 Done-when met y/n; stays open y/n> - gitleaks rc <n>)`. Then the sections: Step 0 (sha256s, slot count), REFUSE counts, PINS (start and verdict), instrument and load, Checks 1-9 each with the FAIL clock and evidence path, findings `B734-n` (severity, class SAME or DIFFERENT for a Major with the rule applied, `path:line` at the head, instrument, FAIL met, plant diff, fix-shape in prose, evidence class MEASURED AT RUNTIME / PROBED / READ ONLY; "none" is valid), the plant table (plant x base x round-1 head x head, right reason), the fresh-battery table, the trailing-comment table, the legitimate-edit table, the mutant kill table, FOR TUESDAY (the verdict in plain words; whether the head-pinned squash can go now and the exact command; what CI still owes; that this is round 2 of 2 and what the cap leaves shipped and ticketed; the open residue as candidate decisions: the unread-body and `with:`-input lane, the `name:`-added-to-an-unnamed-step red, the split ticket key, the ticket move, the stale PR body and the squash wording), FOUND / TESTED / HOW / NOT TESTED / corrections / processes, ports and trees left, **UNMEASURED** (at least: the runner's Python; GitHub's duplicate-key, env-name and forged-`uses:` semantics; whether #221's `api` checks go green on the recomputed merge after #225; the mutants and probes you cut; whole-infra under 3.9.6 if cut). **Last line of STATUS: ONE line, exactly one of:** `VERDICT: B734 pr221 b708/hpsmpoc-353-ci-reader-closure @ 22d5c13 <GO|GO WITH FINDINGS|NO GO|NOT GATED> (round 2 of 2<; conditional: CI pending: names, only when it is><; conditional: CI red, environmental: names, only when it is>; CI <complete|pending: names|red: names>) on main <sha7>` (main by `ls-remote` at verdict), with the findings ids, severities and classes in the line above it (`B734-1 Note`), or `STOPPED: NEEDS TUESDAY <one question>`.

